vided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P10114","text":"Small GTP-binding protein which cycles between a GDP-bound inactive and a GTP-bound active form (PubMed:14966141, PubMed:15342639, PubMed:16246175, PubMed:16540189, PubMed:18930710, PubMed:20159449, PubMed:35293963). In its active form interacts with and regulates several effectors including MAP4K4, MINK1 and TNIK (PubMed:14966141, PubMed:15342639, PubMed:18930710, PubMed:20159449). Part of a signaling complex composed of NEDD4, RAP2A and TNIK which regulates neuronal dendrite extension and arborization during development (PubMed:20159449). More generally, it is part of several signaling cascades and regulates cytoskeletal rearrangements, cell migration, cell adhesion and cell spreading (PubMed:14966141, PubMed:15342639, PubMed:16246175, PubMed:16540189, PubMed:18930710, PubMed:20159449, PubMed:35293963)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}